cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this MuJoCo/MJLab port, please cite this software and the exact
  revision used. Please also cite the SuperMimic paper for the method and
  acknowledge the pinned third-party implementation listed in references.
type: software
title: "SuperMimic-MuJoCo: A MuJoCo/MJLab Port of a Third-Party SuperMimic Implementation"
authors:
  - name: SuperMimic-MuJoCo contributors
version: 0.2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/panhainan2020/SuperMimic-MuJoCo
url: https://github.com/panhainan2020/SuperMimic-MuJoCo
license-url: https://github.com/panhainan2020/SuperMimic-MuJoCo/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
abstract: >-
  Independent MuJoCo/MJLab simulator port based on Chong Zhang's
  supermimic_vibed implementation of SuperMimic. This project supplies
  standalone CPU/CUDA simulation, two G1 robot configurations, and training,
  evaluation and visualization tools. The original method and upstream code
  are credited separately. This is not official code from the paper authors.
  Implementation code is MIT-licensed; assets and other components retain
  their own licenses as documented in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - humanoid control
  - motion tracking
  - MuJoCo
  - MJLab
references:
  - type: article
    title: "SuperMimic: Scaling Humanoid Whole-Body Control with One Differentiable World Model"
